<description>
Extend the bottom source as a two-cell diagonal band upward-right, sliding it right around foreground blockers.

Input structure
- The grid has a dominant background color.
- Exactly one foreground pixel lies on the bottom row; this is the colored source.
- Any other foreground pixels are blockers that remain fixed.

Rule
- Copy the input, then emit the source color upward one row at a time.
- The first row above the source starts a two-cell horizontal band at the source column; each next row shifts that band one column right.
- If the band would touch a blocker in its row, shift it further right until both band cells avoid blockers.
- When such an extra shift leaves a gap from the previous row's band, fill the gap on the previous row with the source color.
- Stop when the band has moved completely past the right edge.

Key insight
- Blockers do not stop the diagonal ray; they push the two-cell-wide band right, and the previous row is widened only enough to keep the trail connected.
</description>
<annotation>
{
  "type": "move_along_path",
  "src": "unique bottom-row foreground source pixel; all other foreground pixels are fixed blockers",
  "path": "diagonal upward-right row sweep: the first two-cell band starts at the source column, each next row normally shifts one column right, and any blocker hit shifts the band further right until clear; stop after the band passes the right edge",
  "trajectory": "paint source color on the band cells, clipped by the right edge; when an extra right shift creates a gap, fill that gap on the previous row",
  "transform": "preserve the source pixel and all blocker pixels"
}
</annotation>
<generation_spec>
```yaml
spec:
  grid: 10x10 [observed]
  background: 0 (black)
  source:
    position: single pixel on bottom row (row 9), col 0-4 [observed] to allow multi-row trail
    color: 2 (red) [observed]; unique in input (appears exactly once)
  blockers:
    count: 0-3; color 1 (blue) [observed]; single color per grid
    placement: every blocker must lie on the actual (possibly already-deflected) diagonal path
    shape: 1-2 horizontally adjacent cells per row; at most 2 distinct rows carry blockers
  trail:
    direction: upward-right diagonal; 2-cell-wide horizontal band per row
    deflection: when band hits blocker, shift right until clear; fill gap on previous row
    termination: band exits right edge (col 9); traverses 6-9 rows above source
    extra_shifts: 0-2 per grid; connector fills 0-3 cells total

generation_strategy:
  approach: path-first
  steps:
    1. Create 10x10 grid of background (0).
    2. Pick source_col in 0-4; place source_color (2) at (9, source_col).
    3. Simulate the upward-right diagonal band from the source:
       - First band at row 8, left=source_col. Each subsequent row shifts left+1.
       - Before placing each band, optionally insert 1-2 horizontally adjacent blockers
         at that row at the natural band position (or the already-shifted position),
         forcing further rightward deflection. Use 0-3 total blocker cells across 0-2 rows.
       - Fill connector cells on previous row when a gap is created.
       - Stop when left >= 10.
    4. Record the full output with trail painted. Remove trail cells to get the input
       (keep source pixel and blocker pixels only).
    5. Validate: all blockers are encountered during traversal; source color appears
       once in input; trail reaches right edge.
```
